    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against weak opposing arms, specifically targeting the vulnerable profiles of Paredes and Gasser. **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) is our unequivocal anchor, benefiting from an elite combination of a 4.94 xERA matchup and a massive 19% boost from the SP skill adjustment. Joining him as a primary engine is **Gabriel Moreno** (69.96), whose 4th-order placement and positive park factors solidify his status as our most efficient catcher play. While **James Wood** (65.62) faces a trickier matchup against Martinez, his elite .404 xwOBA and the 10% boost from leadoff duties provide the necessary floor to remain a cornerstone of today's scoring core.\n\nThe optimizer heavily weighted our stolen base threats to mitigate scarcity; **Brice Turang** (68.34) stands out as a high-leverage start, with a 4% bonus derived from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, creating a prime environment for base-path aggression. Conversely, the most difficult bench decision involved **Max Muncy** (47.03), who narrowly missed the cut. Despite favorable park factors and a BvP edge, **Muncy** ultimately fell short of the starting rotation due to an unfavorable 9th-order batting slot which heavily penalized his efficiency score. We are also monitoring **Tyler Soderstrom** (47.73), who faces a significant challenge against Detmers; while the 10% park boost keeps him in the lineup, his negative SP skill adjustment makes him a high-variance play to watch throughout the afternoon. We remain cautious with **Alex Freeland** (56.52) and **Kyle Karros** (47.89), both of whom are suppressed by their low lineup positions, though the wind conditions in **Karros**'s park offer a narrow path to outperforming his sub-50 projection.",
